Initialize Pointers: Set odd to the 1st node (head), even to the 2nd node (head->next), and save evenHead to reconnect later.

Separate Odd and Even Nodes: Traverse the list using even and even->next; point odd->next to the next odd node and even->next to the next even node, then advance both.

Join Chains: Connect the tail of the odd chain (odd->next) to the saved head of the even chain (evenHead).

Return Result: Return head, which now points to the newly reordered list.



Code :-
class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* oddEvenList(ListNode* head) {
        if (head == NULL || head->next == NULL)
            return head;

        ListNode* odd = head;
        ListNode* even = head->next;
        ListNode* evenHead = even;

        while (even != NULL && even->next != NULL) {
            odd->next = even->next;
            odd = odd->next;

            even->next = odd->next;
            even = even->next;
        }

        odd->next = evenHead;
        return head;
    }
};
